Explanation:
Continuous CHange Detection ans Classification characterizes spectral trajectories of Landsat pixel values under the assumption that spectral signal is stable along a given coefficient.
-{\textgreater} stabilizes annual noise, more sophisticated than 3 year densification.
quote:
``Tasseled-cap indices explain a majority of the variance in the Landsat spectral space (Huang et al., 2002) and normalized burn ratio is sensitive to major forest disturbances'' (Bell et al., 2024, p. 3)
Explanation:
T-Cap indices quite useful.
},
	file = {1-s2.0-S0378112724005516-main:/home/bene/Desktop/repos/literature/1-s2.0-S0378112724005516-main.pdf:application/pdf},
